{"author":{"id":"b409816c5cd5ab140d1d52eb33aace35de44952bb794b19806fd57f6ecb1ace9"},"ops":[{"type":1,"timestamp":1793962013,"nonce":"I2AS1lcRA13lU5Dhd/mPSBFetok=","title":"Cranelift dumps collide between source functions and OSR helper variants","message":"DUMP_CRANELIFT/DUMP_VCODE label functions using the HIR source name, so the ordinary body and multiple state-frame OSR helpers all appear as lua$main$1 in collatz. A consumer keyed by that name silently overwrites earlier emissions. In one of the normal-OSR snapshot-preserving captures, the candidate emits the ordinary zero-arg function, a one-frame-pointer helper reading two live-ins, then another helper reading six. The baseline emits the first two only. Comparing the last occurrence falsely reports a register/frame/code difference for the same source function.\n\nPreserve all emissions and identify helpers by FuncId/site/loop ordinal in diagnostic labels. Existing compile_osr_layout and compile_osr_func_id hold that information during emission. Keep source-name substring filtering useful. This is diagnostic identity debt; do not infer selected native entry from the last dumped helper.\n\nEvidence /private/tmp/zyntax-mark-filter/full/nuc: original hot-collatz-*-1.trace files. inspect_emissions.py matches by source name, ABI signature and entry-frame offsets, retaining all duplicates rather than overwriting them. All48 common native variants across pipeline/tokenize/collatz/op_overload and three pairs match opcode/register/spill sequences after a bijective embedded-address mapping validated by variation across same-binary ASLR runs; one extra six-live-in collatz helper is recorded separately. Sixteen additional snapshot-preserving TRACE_INTERP runs show outer-loop/two-live-in OSR transfers in both arms, with some direct native calls. No transfer to that extra inner helper was observed in these instrumented runs, which can themselves perturb scheduling.\n\nRelated e9e16f2 scan-filter experiment and ef50db3 ordering issue. No production diagnostic-label change is included in the scan-filter candidate. Full pinned official TS corpus remains required before a separate shared-compiler change is committed.","files":null}]}